module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.rest_success_and_decode_are_separately_true

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data rest_success_and_decode_are_separately_true: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "rest_success_and_decode_are_separately_true" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "REST success and REST semantic result are separately true and only one of them is checked (an operation is declared, hermetically witnessed and green; a wet call to it classifies the exchange as SUCCESS because a 200 did come back, and the declared record is Null - so a consumer reads a successful fetch that fetched nothing)",
    "FOUND 2026-09-10 BY A PROBE BUILT TO ANSWER A DIFFERENT QUESTION, on gunbc#10964. A review asked for the GitHub contents API's `size` field to be typed as a std.measure ByteSize. Shipping that on a hermetic green was refusable on its face - a mock_response is authored .dag data - so the wet path was run instead, with a real token: GET https://api.github.com/repos/biomejs/biome/contents/.github/workflows/main.yml at ref 47d7383d049b36ff8eaba50912176928143dd9e9. It refused inside the classifier with TypeError \"cannot access field 'encoding' on Null\". ",
    "THE MECHANISM IS NOT ESTABLISHED AND THIS ROW DOES NOT NAME ONE. What is established is the SYMPTOM at one boundary: a wet 200 did not become the declared record. Naming the JSON decoder would be naming one candidate stage among several - acquisition, body reading, request composition and projection are all still live - and an error class that asserts an unisolated cause sends its own repair to the wrong place. The honest claim is the absence: no wet REST read in this corpus has evidence of producing a value. That is what the row carries. ",
    "FIVE CONTROLS, RECORDED SO THE NEXT READER DOES NOT RE-RUN THEM, and the last two narrow the fault rather than merely ruling things out. (1) Reverting the field to a plain Int does not change it, which rules out the Measure the review asked for. (2) A throwaway operation whose entire response type is a single `sha: String` does not change it, which rules out field-set strictness against a body carrying a dozen unnamed fields. (3) The exchange classified as RestExchangeSucceeded rather than a transport arm, which rules out network and credentials. (4) THE SAME CALL WITH A NONEXISTENT REF - forty zeros - returns 404 and becomes a typed RestExchangeStatusRefused carrying status 404. Since the file exists on the default branch, a dropped `ref` would have returned 200; so the query parameter IS applied, the path and auth are correct, and the status-refusal path works end to end. (5) The same symptom reproduces on a SECOND, structurally different operation - GET /search/code, whose response is a page record rather than a file record - refusing with \"cannot access field 'incomplete_results' on Null\", so it is not one operation's declaration. ",
    "WHAT THE CONTROLS LEAVE STANDING, stated as a narrowing rather than a cause: acquisition reached the service, the request was composed correctly including its query, authentication was accepted, and a refusal status becomes a typed refusal. What has no evidence of working is the step between a 200 body and a declared record - body reading or projection - and no receipt in hand distinguishes those two. THE PRINTED LOG LINE DOES NOT CARRY THE QUERY, which is why control (4) exists at all: the URL rendered in the run log stops at the path, so a claim that a ref was applied cannot be read off it and had to be established by a discriminating status instead. ",
    "WHAT MAKES THIS GREEN-FOR-THE-WRONG-REASON RATHER THAN MERELY UNDER-COVERED, which is the distinguishing fact and the whole reason it earns a row. A mock_response NEVER PASSES THROUGH THE WIRE PATH: it is authored .dag data published beside the operation and substituted for the exchange. So the hermetic witness and this defect are DISJOINT - not a weak test of the right thing, but a correct test of a different thing. No amount of strengthening the hermetic claims can reach it, and every strengthening makes the coverage look better. ",
    "THE BLAST RADIUS IS EVERY WET REST CONSUMER, and on the evidence available at this writing no wet REST read has passing evidence anywhere in this corpus. gunbc.github_authenticated_user_read is the only other wet-capable consumer and its own annotation states that live GET /user is not executed in the change that added it. gunbc#10923 landed the performer these all sit on under the title \"Give GitHubEffect a REST performer whose shape is hermetically verdicted\" - shape-verdicted and wet-unexercised is exactly this gap, cited here so the next reader does not assume that change covered it. ",
    "RUNG AND CEILING. Found at MITIGATABLE AT BEST: the failure is loud when a consumer touches a field and silent for any consumer that does not - a fold over a decoded list would see an empty list and report a repository with no matching workflow, which is a fabricated observation arriving through the success path. The CEILING is a wet-path admission enrolled as executing evidence, and the TRIGGER is that admission existing, in three stages because the first two are what isolate the stage these controls could not: (a) a CAPTURED 200 receipt carrying body byte count and hash, content type, the requested ref, and which body-read arm ran; (b) a REPLAY of that exact captured body through the production dispatcher, asserting encoding, sha, content and size against a UNIQUE SENTINEL value, so a replay cannot pass on a coincidence; (c) a wet rerun at the same ref. Until that exists, a hermetic green on a REST operation establishes the SHAPE of its response and says nothing about whether a wire body becomes one. ",
    "THE SAME SHAPE ONE LEVEL UP, owed by any queue built over these reads: a decode or projection failure must produce a TYPED RETRY OR REQUEUE disposition and must never be recorded as Succeeded. A work ledger may not admit Leased -> Succeeded without a non-null, schema-valid semantic result AND a durable commit - which is this row's own defect restated as a state machine, and the reason to write the rule before the queue rather than after it. ",
    "THE REVIEW TELL IS A MOCK STANDING WHERE A WET RESULT WAS NEVER OBSERVED: an operation whose only executed evidence is a mock_response, and a PR body that describes what the endpoint returns without a receipt showing the endpoint's bytes becoming the declared value. The authoring tell is the one that produced this row - reaching for a wet run because a hermetic green would not have settled the question being asked. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
